  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Add support for some additional Cisco IKEv2 VIDs",
  "description": "- CISCO-DYNAMIC-ROUTE  \n  Indicates support for IKEv2 Dynamic Routing. Included by default in IKEv2 `IKE_SA_INIT` requests.\n- CISCO-VPN-REV-02  \n  Not so sure about this one. It's also included by default in IKEv2 `IKE_SA_INIT` requests. I suspect it indicates to Cisco peers various internal differences in the IKE implementation which may influence subsequent configuration of the security associations. Recognising the VID and displaying a cleaned-up description still strikes me as better than the current \"_Unknown Vendor ID_\" display, requiring manual inspection of the packet bytes.",
